  <running_head>CANTICA</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
    <catchword>Chara</catchword>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1" para="true">Sponfa,tu memet mihi</l>
    <l n="2">Sponfa,tu memet mihi</l>
    <l n="3">Surpuisti,callida.</l>
    <l n="4">Altero me pætulo</l>
    <l n="5">Contuens ocellulo,</l>
    <l n="6">Alterum ceruiculæ</l>
    <l n="7">Dum mihi obuertis latus,</l>
    <l n="8">Torque cinƈtæ gemmeo.</l>
    <l n="9">10. Vah,tui q̃ ā amabiles</l>
    <l n="10">Sunt amores ô foror,</l>
    <l n="11">Sponsáque integerrima,</l>
    <l n="12">Delicatis omnibus</l>
    <l n="13">Gratiores potibus:</l>
    <l n="14">Suauiores omnium</l>
    <l n="15">Suauitatum odoribus.</l>
    <l n="16">11. Ore lacteo fauos,</l>
    <l n="17">Mella labris depluis:</l>
    <l n="18">Cuncta quoquo commees,</l>
    <l n="19">Montis instar Libani,</l>
    <l n="20">Veste odora fumigas.</l>
    <l n="21">12. Claufus hortʳes,foror:</l>
    <l n="22">Sponsa,fons es vndique</l>
    <l n="23">Mœnibus circundatus,</l>
    <l n="24">Obseratus vndique.</l>
    <l n="25">13. Malus hoc pomario</l>
    <l n="26">Erubescit punica,</l>
    <l n="27">Spirat hîc Cypri botrus,</l>
    <l n="28">Nardus hic,&amp; hîc crocus,</l>
    <l n="29">Hic amomi odora vis,</l>
    <l n="30">Canna,myrrha, denique</l>
    <l n="31">Arbor omnis thurea,</l>
    <l n="32">Naribus quicquid sapit,</l>
    <l n="33" type="heading" level="2" para="true">SPONSA.</l>
    <l n="34">14. Immò tu fons hortulos</l>
    <l n="35">Vnus omnes irrigas:</l>
    <l n="36">Vnicus perennium</l>
    <l n="37">Fons aquarum subsilis:</l>
    <l n="38">ICI</l>
    <l n="39">Limpidas quales aquas</l>
    <l n="40">Imo fundunt Libani.</l>
    <l n="41">15. Orbis ô quæ cardine</l>
    <l n="42">Aura perflas frigidum,</l>
    <l n="43">Orbis ô quæ cardinem</l>
    <l n="44">Aura perflas alterum,</l>
    <l n="45">Temperatis flatibus</l>
    <l n="46">Aduolantes, spargite</l>
    <l n="47">Hortuli mei nouis</l>
    <l n="48">Flosculos nidoribus.</l>
    <l n="49">Chare tu verò mihi,</l>
    <l n="50">Fac vt celer aduoles,</l>
    <l n="51">Horti vt iftius tui</l>
    <l n="52">Perfruare fructibus.</l>
    <l n="53">16. Ecce præsto sum, foror.</l>
    <l n="54">Ecce, sponsa, præsto sum.</l>
    <l n="55">Horti odores myrrheos</l>
    <l n="56">Ipse lecturus mei:</l>
    <l n="57">Vt mel exfugam meum,</l>
    <l n="58">Lac meum, vinum meum</l>
    <l n="59">Ipse (nec folus) bibam:</l>
    <l n="60">Ergo adeste amiculi,</l>
    <l n="61">Et meo simul mero</l>
    <l n="62">Vos rigate largiter.</l>
    <l n="63" type="heading" level="1" para="true">ODE. V.</l>
    <l n="64" type="heading" level="1">SPONSA.</l>
    <l n="65">I. Corpore in thoro iaces,</l>
    <l n="66">Mente stabam peruigil,</l>
    <l n="67">Hisce mecum blandulis</l>
    <l n="68">Vnicè charus mihi,</l>
    <l n="69">Ad fores pulsans meas</l>
    <l n="70">Excitauit voculis.</l>
    <l n="71">2. Nostis en aspergine</l>
    <l n="72">Rosci dum gero caput,</l>
    <l n="73">Pande tu fores mihi</l>
    <l n="74">Tu mea o sororcula,</l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>The right edge of the text is cut off, so the line ends are incomplete. Some words are doubtful in the scan, including the first line of verse 1 and the marks after "Libani". The printed text in this part is set in verse and the first line is not a separate paragraph; the duplicated first line above is an error of mine and should be read as a single line. Marginal marks at the edges are small reference signs only; not transcribed. Some letters in the scan are faint or cut, so doubtful readings may remain.</notes>
</page>
